Byte for byte. `tools/vendored_test.py` checks these digests, and
`tools/refresh.py` is what fetched them -- run weekly, opening a
pull request when the release moves, so a copy that has drifted is
a failing check rather than a surprise.

The licence file is here because every one of these says 'See the
file LICENSE.txt for your full rights' in its first five lines. It
is GPL-3, the same licence this package is under, and it is taken
from the release the drivers came from rather than copied from
anywhere else -- so it is the text those files were published with.
The copyright is Tom Keffer's and the contributors', as each file's
own header says.

